#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Lane D Accept (plan §3 conventions, §3.1, invariant 10, §17.2).

    accept <WP> [--evidence FILE] [--root R]
        invariant10 -> pytest tests/accept/<wp>/ -> stub_scan over PATHS
        -> make laned-e2e (when the Makefile defines it) -> evidence
        With --evidence, pytest and e2e see LANED_EVIDENCE=<abs FILE>: the
        WP's own tests verify the evidence content (plan §3, §17.1 L4).
    accept <WP> --expect-fail [--root R]
        tests-only PRs for an unbuilt WP: tests collected and failing for a
        right reason only
    accept <WP> --verification --base REF --head REF [--root R]
        the run for MODE tests-only: MODE verification when it applies (rules
        below), else exactly --expect-fail
    accept <WP> --tests-correction --base REF --head REF [--root R]
        tests-only PRs for a WP already built on BASE (see MODE rules below)
    accept <WP> --check-pr --base REF --head REF [--pr-wps WP,WP...] [--root R]
        rule 1 and the WP's PATHS over `git diff --name-only BASE...HEAD`;
        prints the MODE the PR job runs next (rules below); --pr-wps names
        every laned:<WP> label of the PR (BATCH and BATCH IMPLEMENTATION
        rules below);
        for a review WP RV<n>: MODE review iff the diff is exactly an add or
        modify of evidence/rv<n>.md (no tests run)
    accept <WP>[,<WP>...] --cross --base REF --head REF [--root R]
        cross-WP regressions (CROSS rule below); prints `CROSS <WP> PASS|KNOWN|FAIL`
    accept [<WP>] --freshness --base REF --head REF --main REF [--root R]
        stale-base guard (FRESHNESS rule below); prints `FRESH ...` or
        `STALE BASE: update-branch and re-run` (exit 1)
    accept selftest
        offline check of the review, tests-correction, verification,
        evidence, cross and freshness modes
    accept --gate <STAGE> [--root R]
        evidence/gates/<stage>.json: right stage, every check passed

MODE rules of --check-pr (the PR job runs the named mode next):
    MODE implementation   the diff has no tests/accept/ path and stays inside
                          the WP's PATHS -> full Accept
    MODE tests-only       the diff touches only tests/accept/<wp>/ and BASE has
                          no implementation of the WP (no L2 commit on BASE's
                          first-parent line: a commit after the one adding
                          PATHS that changes non-test files, all inside PATHS)
                          -> --verification (below), which is --expect-fail
                          over the WP's whole test dir unless the PR is a
                          verification PR
    MODE verification     printed by --verification, not by --check-pr: a
                          tests-only PR for a VERIFICATION WP, one whose row
                          only asserts properties of code another WP already
                          built. It applies iff (0) the WP is listed in
                          scripts/laned/verification_wps at BASE (RV5: the
                          PR cannot declare it; an unlisted WP always runs
                          --expect-fail), (a) BASE has no L2 commit for
                          the WP, (b) every non-test entry of the WP's PATHS
                          already exists on BASE (an exact file; some file
                          under a dir/ entry; some file matching a glob) and
                          (c) the full Accept (invariant10, pytest, stub_scan
                          over PATHS, e2e) passes on the PR's tests over BASE's
                          code. Then it prints `MODE verification` and passes;
                          the ledger records mode `verification` with
                          `tests_tree` (tree sha of tests/accept/<wp>/ at HEAD).
                          A PATHS entry missing on BASE (or a PATHS file with no
                          non-test entry) never gives verification; any failing
                          Accept step falls back to --expect-fail semantics
                          (at least one right-reason failure), recorded as
                          mode `expect-fail`, so a normal tests-only PR still
                          works. On merge the status board treats the merge
                          commit (the first first-parent commit changing only
                          tests/accept/<wp>/ whose test dir has that
                          tests_tree) as both L1 and L2 for the WP; the
                          push-to-main Accept run then gives L3 as usual.
    MODE tests-correction the diff touches only tests/accept/<wp>/ and BASE
                          already has the WP's implementation (L2 commit found)
                          -> --tests-correction: every test file the PR does
                          NOT change must pass against BASE's implementation;
                          the test files it changes run in expect-fail
                          classification: each failure must be for a right
                          reason (it is pending a follow-up implementation
                          PR), and all of them passing is fine. Any
                          wrong-reason failure, or any failure in an
                          unchanged test file, fails the PR.
                          A test file counts as changed when the PR adds or
                          edits it, or any file in its static closure inside
                          tests/accept/<wp>/: modules it imports (relative,
                          or absolute resolving into the WP dir; transitive),
                          ancestor conftest.py / __init__.py in the WP dir,
                          and non-.py files under the WP dir named by a string
                          constant in that closure (basename, WP-dir-relative
                          path, or a containing directory such as "fixtures").
    MODE evidence         the diff only adds or modifies evidence files named
                          by `--evidence <file>` in the WP's §3.0 Accept cell
                          (plan at BASE); check-pr prints `EVIDENCE <file>`
                          per file -> `accept <WP> --evidence <file>` for each,
                          recorded in the ledger as mode `evidence` with the
                          file's blob sha (the push to main then re-runs it as
                          push/accept --evidence, which is what L4 reads).
                          A declared evidence file together with any other
                          path, a deletion, or an evidence/-only diff naming a
                          file the Accept cell does not declare (and PATHS do
                          not cover) -> FAIL evidence.
    MODE review           RV<n> label, the diff is exactly evidence/rv<n>.md

BATCH rule (plan rev6.2 item (h)): a tests-only PR may carry several WPs'
tests. When --pr-wps names more than one label and the diff is only under
tests/accept/, check-pr requires: every path is inside some
tests/accept/<wp>/ dir; each such dir belongs to a label of the set; each
label's dir is in the diff; every label is a WP (no RV<n>); and either no WP
of the set is built on BASE (L2 commit) -> `BATCH <WPs>` + `MODE tests-only`,
or (plan rev6.3 (b)) every WP of the set is built and there are at most 3 ->
`BATCH <WPs>` + `MODE tests-correction` (a batch of corrections, each WP run
in --tests-correction on its own). Otherwise `FAIL rule1: batch-<reason>: ...`
with reason non-wp-label, duplicate-label, stray-tests, unlabelled-tests,
label-without-tests, built-wp (built and unbuilt WPs mixed) or too-many. The
PR job then runs each WP's --verification (its own TESTS-TREE in the ledger)
or --tests-correction separately and fails when any WP fails. Code + tests is
still rule 1 (one diff never mixes them). A single label keeps the one-WP rule
(another WP's tests dir fails rule 1).

BATCH IMPLEMENTATION rule (plan rev6.3 item (b)): when --pr-wps names more
than one label and the diff has no tests/accept/ path, check-pr requires
    at most 3 WPs (too-many), all laned:<WP> (non-wp-label), no two naming the
    same dir (duplicate-label);
    (3) every WP's tests are on BASE: tests/accept/<wp>/PATHS and a test file
        (no-tests);
    (2) no WP of the set depends on another, directly or transitively, by the
        Depends cells of the §3.0 WP tables in the plan at BASE (dependency); a
        WP whose row or table has no Depends column cannot be told and is
        refused (deps-unknown);
    (1) the WPs' PATHS sets (at BASE) are disjoint: no pair of entries can
        match one path (globs judged conservatively) and no file at BASE or
        HEAD matches two sets (overlapping-paths);
    scope: every changed file is in exactly one batch WP's PATHS (a file in
        none, a PROTECTED file, or a scripts/laned/ file outside W0c's ->
        `FAIL paths: batch-out-of-scope`; a file in two -> `FAIL paths:
        batch-ambiguous`), and every WP owns a changed file
        (label-without-changes).
Refusals print `FAIL rule1: batch-<reason>: ...` (scope ones `FAIL paths:`).
When it holds check-pr prints `BATCH <WPs>`, `SCOPE <WP> <n> file(s)` per WP
and `MODE implementation`, identically for each label; the PR job then runs
each WP's own full Accept, records one ledger row per WP and runs CROSS with
the whole set as the PR's own WPs. On main the squash merge is each WP's L2
commit: lanedlib.impl_commit_index also takes a commit whose files are each
matched exactly once by the WP's own PATHS and at most 2 other WPs' PATHS (at
the ref), each matching some (lanedlib.is_batch_impl_commit).

COUPLED rule (orchestrator decision 2026-11-23, lane D rev6.10-rev6.12): a
declared coupled set (one line of scripts/laned/coupled_batches, read at BASE
only; scripts/laned/ is W0c-only, so a PR can never declare its own set) is
WPs whose producer, audit and replay must change together and whose PATHS
overlap. When --pr-wps is EXACTLY such a set (no subset, no superset) the
BATCH IMPLEMENTATION rule applies without its size cap, its dependency check
(2) and its disjoint-PATHS check (1). Everything else holds: laned:<WP>
labels only, no duplicate dir, every member's tests on BASE (no-tests), every
changed file inside some member's PATHS (a file in several is owned by each;
none, PROTECTED or a non-W0c scripts/laned/ file -> `FAIL paths:
batch-out-of-scope`), every member owning a changed file
(label-without-changes). It prints `COUPLED <WPs>` before the BATCH / SCOPE /
MODE lines, and the PR job runs every member's full Accept, ledger row and
CROSS as for any batch. Any other overlap is refused as before. On main the
squash merge is each member's L2 commit (lanedlib.is_coupled_impl_commit:
no tests/accept/ file, every file in the members' PATHS union, every member's
PATHS matching a file).

CROSS rule (the PR job runs it after the PR's own WP steps, every mode but
review): a WP other than the PR's own WP(s) is re-accepted when
    (a) it is built on BASE: tests/accept/<wp>/PATHS exists at BASE and either
        BASE's first-parent line has its L2 commit (lanedlib.impl_commit_index,
        the board's L2 rule), or it is a verification WP (listed in
        scripts/laned/verification_wps at BASE) whose non-test PATHS all exist
        at BASE (the board's L2 via verification; without the ledger its green
        verification run is not re-checked, nor is the board's L1 ledger
        precondition, so a WP in doubt is included), and
    (b) its tests depend on `git diff --name-only BASE...HEAD`: the diff touches
        a global input (pyproject.toml, uv.lock, tests/conftest.py, ...), its
        own test dir, a path its PATHS match, a repo module in the static
        import closure of its test dir (AST, transitive through repo modules
        and package __init__.py; absolute imports resolve from the repo root,
        the importing file's dir, tests/accept and tests), or a path named by a
        string constant in its test files ("cascade/x/y.json", "chain.toml").
The tests-correction / tests-only / verification WP X of the PR is its own
main step, so X is never a cross WP. A cross WP runs invariant 10, pytest over
its test dir (all cross WPs in one pytest run, split only where two
non-package test dirs share a module basename) and stub_scan over its PATHS;
no e2e (the main step ran it). A failure the junit report cannot attribute to
one WP fails every WP of that run.
A cross WP whose pytest fails on HEAD is re-run at BASE (a temporary detached
worktree of BASE, same LANED_PYTEST_CMD, removed afterwards) and compared per
junit test id:
    CROSS <WP> KNOWN  every test failing on HEAD also fails on BASE (already
                      red on main; printed with the ids; does not fail the job)
    CROSS <WP> FAIL   a test that passes on BASE fails on HEAD (a regression),
                      or either run is not plain test failures (no report,
                      unattributed failures, a collection error, nothing
                      collected): fails closed.

FRESHNESS rule (the PR job's last step, RV5): BASE is the base the run tested
(the merge commit's first parent), MAIN is origin/main fetched at job time.
BASE == MAIN is fresh. Otherwise, with MB = merge-base(BASE, MAIN), the PR is
STALE when its diff (BASE...HEAD) and main's diff (MB..MAIN) interact, in the
PR's tree or in MAIN's: a path both touch; a changed module of one side whose
static import closure reaches a changed path of the other; or a WP test dir
that depends (CROSS rule (b)) on both diffs. Unrelated main commits leave the
PR fresh. The loop must update-branch and re-run a STALE PR before merging.

The pytest command is `uv run --frozen pytest` unless LANED_PYTEST_CMD is set
(shlex-split). It always runs with cwd = --root. Exit 0 means pass.
"""

